Best = 200, 9 of 10 insns identical. Only diff: target starts `lsls r1,#16; asrs r1,#16` (signed entry conv), agbcc emits `lsls; lsrs` (zero-extend). Rest matches exactly: mvns r1,r1; adds r1,#1; lsls r1,#16; asrs r1,#16; bl sub_0800F9E4. Best source:
```c
void sub_0800F9E4(s32, s16);
void sub_0801057C(s32 arg0, s16 arg1) { sub_0800F9E4(arg0, (s16)(~arg1 + 1)); }
```
Reason it can't be fixed by source: the entry sign-extension's high bits are dead because the value is truncated to s16 for the callee, so agbcc's combine always rewrites sign_extend->zero_extend. Tried: `-arg1` (510, rsbs), s32 param + `s16 x=arg1` + `~x+1` (200, same lsrs), `s32 v=(s16)(~arg1+1)` with callee s32 (200, same), s16 local `v=~arg1+1; call(v)` (200, same). search_flags: -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os/-fno-strength-reduce all 200 — flags are not the cause. Needs either a source trick keeping the sign live past the truncation (would add insns) or a different compiler revision. sub_080105B8 is the identical s8 twin (also 200, same lsrs-vs-asrs).

